          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 32,
            "column": 4
          },
          "text": "Developer Mode Reality Check"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": {
        "line": 34,
        "column": 1
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 34,
            "column": 1
          },
          "text": "Apple does not provide a public API to read the iOS Developer Mode toggle. This plugin uses indirect heuristics such as debugger attachment and development provisioning indicators. Treat them as risk signals, not proof."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": {
        "line": 36,
        "column": 1
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 36,
            "column": 1
          },
          "text": "Tools like iMyFone AnyTo often rely on Developer Mode and companion apps distributed outside the App Store. Combine native checks with server-side fraud rules."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "location": {
        "line": 38,
        "column": 1
      },
      "depth": 2,
      "blocks": [
